// EXPECT: REJECT
// ADR 0043 — writing to `count` while a shared borrow of it
// is still live is an error.
//
// The write at `count := 99` falls between the borrow's creation
// and its last use at `print(*r)`. Rejected with E0007.
//
// Before ADR 0043 this program compiled and printed 99 — a
// soundness hole. The mutation invalidated the reference held
// in `r`, and `print(*r)` observed the mutated value through a
// borrow that was live across the write.

proc main
    var count := 10
    val r := &count

    count := 99             // E0007: `r` is live here
    print(*r)               // last use of `r` — too late

    print(count)